// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/trinet/e3_tx_hold_model_ax7203.t27 -- pre-registration: the E3 transmit edge timing at the
; FPGA's output buffers, in nextpnr-xilinx's own delay model, for the routed e3z netlist
; The one source for this check. conformance/e3_tx_hold_from_spec.mjs compiles this file with the
; t27 compiler (wasm), evaluates every test block below, checks the pinned repo files, reads back the
; constants it repeats from the E3 spec, the RTL and the bitstream record, and writes
; conformance/e3_tx_hold_params.py, which the runner conformance/e3_tx_hold_model.py reads.
; `--check` fails on drift. Written 2026-09-27T23:06:06Z (date -u), before any run of the runner and
; before any SDF of e3z existed. ASCII, English.

; WHY. NODE_ETHERNET_PLAN.md, "The TX edge timing on the board": TXD and TX_CTL change some ns after
; the TXC falling edge, through TX_DLY kept LUT1 stages per pin, and "no tool in this flow reports"
; how many. If it is under the PHY's hold time, the last FCS nibble goes out as an error and the
; board run reads H2. The bench stands in 3 ns for it. nextpnr-xilinx can write an SDF of the routed
; design (--sdf): its own delay per net and per cell, from the prjxray timing classes. That is a
; model, not the board, but it is the number this flow has and nobody has read yet.

; WHAT RUNS. nextpnr-xilinx NEXTPNR_BIN (sha pinned) on the e3z synthesized netlist BUILD_DIR/node.json
; with the e3z build's own arguments (chipdb, XDC, --freq, --seed, --placer, --router,
; --timing-allow-fail) plus --sdf, into WORK_DIR. The run is accepted as e3z only if the FASM it
; writes is byte-equal to BUILD_DIR/node.fasm (FASM_SHA256): same placement, same routing, the one
; whose bitstream is PAYLOAD_SHA256. Then the runner walks the SDF back from the input pin I of the
; output buffer of each of the six TX pads to a flip-flop: interconnect delays, LUT pin-to-output
; delays, the flip-flop's clock-to-Q, and the clock net's delay into that flip-flop's clock pin.
; For a TX data pin p (TXD0..3, TX_CTL) that sum is D_p. For TXC it is C_fall along the branch from
; the rising-edge flip-flop tq_p (TXC falls at the RXC rising edge, when TXD and TX_CTL also launch)
; and C_rise along the branch from the falling-edge flip-flop tq_n.

; THE CHECK, per data pin p, in picoseconds:
;   hold_fall  = D_p - C_fall                          must be >= HOLD_MIN_PS
;   setup_rise = RXC_HIGH_MIN_PS + C_rise - D_p        must be >= SETUP_MIN_PS
; hold_fall is the time TX_EN xor TX_ER of the previous nibble stays after the TXC falling edge at
; the output buffers. setup_rise is the time the new nibble is there before the next TXC rising
; edge, with RXC's high time at its RGMII minimum (40 % of 40 ns). The walk must find, for each data
; pin, exactly TX_DLY LUTs between the flip-flop and the buffer, and for TXC exactly one LUT with
; two flip-flop branches.
;   PASS       every data pin meets both.
;   FAIL       some pin misses one: the model predicts the H2 failure mode.
;   NO VERDICT the FASM differs, a pinned file or binary differs, or the walk does not find the
;              structure above. Nothing is concluded then.

; PREDICTION. PASS. A guess, information only, not part of the verdict: hold_fall between
; GUESS_HOLD_LO_PS and GUESS_HOLD_HI_PS on every pin (the RTL comment's 0.3 to 1 ns per stage, less
; the TXC path's one LUT).

; WHAT IT DOES NOT SAY. Anything about the board: the model has one corner and the SDF carries one
; number per arc, so a real hold check (fastest data against slowest clock) is not made; the output
; buffers, the pads, the board traces and the PHY's input delays are outside it (the six pins share
; IOSTANDARD LVCMOS33, SLEW FAST and default drive, so their buffers are alike, not measured); the
; KSZ9031's TX pad-skew registers are left at reset values by E3. A PASS says the design's intent
; (data after the falling edge, well before the rising one) survived place and route in the tool's
; own numbers. It moves nothing in the E3 spec and changes no E3 verdict.

module trinet_e3_tx_hold_model_ax7203;

